teFormat":null},"bibNumber":null,"otherIdentifiers":null,"refsToItem":null,"rightsHolder":[],"relations":null,"source":null,"numberOfPages":null,"number":null,"index":false,"indexPages":"0","withImages":true,"professors":"Μαρία Ρούσσου, Αναπληρώτρια Καθηγήτρια, Τμήμα Πληροφορικής και Τηλεπικοινωνιών, ΕΚΠΑ","numberOfReferences":57,"abstractText":[{"key":"el","value":"Τα Άτομα με Αναπηρία (ΑμεΑ) συναντούν ποικίλα προβλήματα αυτονομίας σε αρκετές \nχώρες του κόσμου. Ένα μέρος αυτών, οι άνθρωποι με οπτική αναπηρία, δεν μπορεί να \nδιασχίσει πολλές φορές τον δρόμο, μιας και δε δύναται να αναγνωρίσει πού είναι το \nαπέναντι φανάρι και αν είναι πράσινο ή κόκκινο. Σαφώς η κοινωνία έχει κάνει προόδους \nστο θέμα αυτό, αλλά προς το παρόν δεν έχει εξαλείψει το πρόβλημα. \nΣτο πλαίσιο αντιμετώπισης αυτού, σχεδιάστηκε και αναπτύχθηκε εφαρμογή για κινητές \nσυσκευές με λειτουργικό σύστημα Android, της οποίας κύριος στόχος είναι η υποστήριξη \nτυφλών χρηστών κατά τη διάσχιση δρόμων. Η εφαρμογή λειτουργεί ως εξής:  \n• Για γνωστή διαδρομή, ο χρήστης ανοίγει την κάμερα και πατά σε ένα κουμπί \nστην οθόνη, ώστε η εφαρμογή να αναγνωρίζει και να ανακοινώνει φωνητικά και \nαπτικά την κατάσταση του φαναριού στην απέναντι πλευρά του δρόμου. \n• Για άγνωστη διαδρομή, η εφαρμογή εντοπίζει τις θέσεις διαβάσεων και \nφαναριών, και οι δονήσεις εντείνονται όσο ο χρήστης πλησιάζει σε κάποιο από \nαυτά.   \nΗ εφαρμογή υλοποιήθηκε στο Android Studio με γλώσσα προγραμματισμού Kotlin, \nαξιοποιώντας τα εργαλεία Roboflow και Mendeley Data για την εκπαίδευση του μοντέλου \nανίχνευσης, καθώς και το OpenStreetMap για τον εντοπισμό υποδομών διαβάσεων και \nφαναριών. Το αποτέλεσμα είναι μια λειτουργική εφαρμογή η οποία, παρά τα περιθώρια \nπεραιτέρω βελτίωσης, επιτυγχάνει τους βασικούς στόχους για τους οποίους \nσχεδιάστηκε."},{"key":"en","value":"People with disabilities encounter various autonomy challenges in many countries around \nthe world. Among them, individuals with visual impairments are often unable to cross the \nroad safely, as they cannot identify the location of the traffic light on the opposite side nor \ndetermine whether it is green or red. While society has made progress in addressing this \nissue, the problem has not yet been fully resolved. \nTo address this, an Android mobile application was designed and developed, with the \nprimary goal of supporting blind users when crossing pedestrian roads. The application \noperates as follows: \n• For a familiar route, the user opens the camera and presses a button on the \nscreen, prompting the application to recognize and announce the state of the \ntraffic light on the opposite side of the road, both through audio feedback via \nthe screen reader and haptic vibration. \n• For an unfamiliar route, the application detects the locations of crossings and \ntraffic lights, with vibrations intensifying as the user approaches one of them. \nThe application was implemented in Android Studio using the Kotlin programming \nlanguage, leveraging Roboflow and Mendeley Data for training the detection model, as \nwell as OpenStreetMap for locating pedestrian infrastructure. The result is a functional \napplication that, despite room for further improvement, achieves the core objectives for \nwhich it was designed."}],"authorship":null,"depositDate":{"publicType":"niovity.butterfly.core.ExactDateRange","from":1791849600000,"to":1791935999999,"fromDateFormat":"DD/MM/YYYY","toDateFormat":null},"casAuthors":[{"id":"cas_sdi2200151","storeName":"users","publicType":"CasUser","permissionsGranted":[{"publicType":"niovity.butterfly.core.security.ContainerAndUnitPermissionGrant","permission":"APPEND","containerCoords":"uoadl:1081404","unitCoords":null}],"isEnabled":true,"fromCAS":true,"favourites":[],"allowBackofficeLogin":false,"cas.givenName":[{"key":"el","value":"ΔΗΜΗΤΡΑ"},{"key":"en","value":"DIMITRA"}],"cas.sn":[{"key":"el","value":"ΠΟΛΙΤΗ"},{"key":"en","value":"POLITI"}],"cas.displayName":[{"key":"el","value":"ΔΗΜΗΤΡΑ ΠΟΛΙΤΗ"},{"key":"en","value":"DIMITRA POLITI"}],"cas.eduPersonAffiliation":["student"],"cas.mail":"sdi2200151@di.uoa.gr","cas.telephone":null,"cas.eduPersonOrgDN":"dc=uoa,dc=gr","cas.dn":null,"cas.uid":"sdi2200151","cas.title":[{"key":"el","value":"undergraduate"},{"key":"en","value":"undergraduate"}],"cas.eduPersonPrimaryOrgUnit":null,"cas.eduPersonPrimaryAffiliation":"student","cas.eduPersonOrgUnitDN":["ou=inftel,ou=schools,dc=uoa,dc=gr"],"selfDeposit.rolesAndUnits":[{"publicType":"CasAuthorizationRecord","affiliation":"student","orgUnitDn":"ou=inftel,ou=schools,dc=uoa,dc=gr","butterflyRole":"UNVERIFIED_STUDENT","academicUnit":{"id":"1062569","storeName":"uoadl","publicType":"Unit","parents":[{"id":"1062563","storeName":"uoadl","publicType":"Unit","parents":[{"id":"__UNIT","storeName":"uoadl","publicType":"Unit"}],"title":[{"key":"el","value":"Σχολή Θετικών Επιστημών"},{"key":"en","value":"School of Science"}],"contactInfo":null,"isActive":true,"publish":"true","published":true,"unitType":"SCHOOL","notificationEmails":null,"notificationEmailsForBooks":null,"notificationEmailsForArticleOrders":null,"notificationEmailsForResearchDatasets":null,"isShownInReports":true,"url":null,"timestamps.createdAt":1453898520000,"timestamps.modifiedAt":1500898905000,"timestamps.publishedAt":1748870891373,"users.createdBy":"users:admin","users.lastModifiedBy":"users:admin","cas.dn":null,"cas.cn":[],"cas.eduOrgSuperiorURI":null,"cas.uoAStructuralType":[]}],"title":[{"key":"el","value":"Τμήμα Πληροφορικής \u0026 Τηλεπικοινωνιών"},{"key":"en","value":"Department of Informatics and Telecommunications"}],"contactInfo":null,"isActive":true,"publish":"true","published":true,"unitType":"DEPARTMENT","notificationEmails":"thesis-notifications@di.uoa.gr","notificationEmailsForBooks":null,"notificationEmailsForArticleOrders":null,"notificationEmailsForResearchDatasets":null,"isShownInReports":true,"url":null,"timestamps.createdAt":1453898527000,"timestamps.modifiedAt":1749102398886,"timestamps.